# DEFECT 081: on Linux x86-64 a C trap with a lease live died at 132 with
# nothing on stderr (panel 175's ffi-pragmatist, 2026-09-23).
#
# Panel 173's handler took SIGTRAP and SIGABRT, and `__builtin_trap()` is SIGTRAP
# on arm64 and SIGILL on x86-64, so the same program named its lease on Darwin
# and Linux arm64 and said nothing on the x86-64 leg. The handler now takes
# SIGILL too. The case asserts the lease line, which is the same text on every
# architecture; under `--sanitize` it is said too, since ASan reports nothing
# for a trap and its death callback never runs.

extern "fixedbugs-c-traps-with-a-lease-live-on-every-architecture.h"
    function c_trap(s: cstr)

function main()
    word = repeat("ab", 4)
    held: cstr @= word.lease()
    c_trap(s: held)
    end_lease(@held)
    print("not reached")
